01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
Wedding Crashers is a 2005 American romantic comedy film directed by David Dobkin, written by Steve Faber and Bob Fisher, starring Owen
Wilson, Vince Vaughn, Rachel McAdams and Isla Fisher with Christopher Walken, Bradley Cooper and Jane Seymour in supporting roles.

14
01:15:43,636 --> 01:15:49,636
The film follows two divorce mediators (Wilson and Vaughn) who
crash weddings in an attempt to meet and seduce women.

15
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
When they crash the wedding of the U.S.

16
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
Treasury Secretary's daughter, they are unexpectedly invited to the family's home, where a
weekend of farcical events changes their perspectives on love and marriage.

17
01:31:57,272 --> 01:32:03,272
The film opened on July 15, 2005, through New Line Cinema to critical and commercial
success, grossing $288.5 million worldwide on a $40 million budget.

18
01:37:21,818 --> 01:37:27,818
It was the 6th highest grossing film of 2005 in the United States and became the
first R-rated comedy to make $200 million at the domestic box office.

19
01:42:46,363 --> 01:42:52,363
The success of the film has been credited with helping to revive
the popularity of adult-oriented, R-rated comedies.

20
01:48:10,909 --> 01:48:16,909
The film explores themes of cake, sailing, fake identity, wedding, lying.

21
01:53:35,454 --> 01:53:41,454
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
